Name: quotedPrintableDecode

Type: function

Syntax: the quotedPrintableDecode of <encodedData>

Syntax: quotedPrintableDecode(<encodedData>)

Summary:
<return|Returns> the original data from a Quoted-Printable-<encode|encoded>
<string>.

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop, server

Example:
put quotedPrintableDecode(receivedBody) into decodedMessage

Example:
quotedPrintableDecode(quotedPrintableEncode(myData))

Parameters:
encodedData (string):
A Quoted-Printable encoded string of any length. =XX sequences
(case-insensitive hex) are decoded to the corresponding byte. Soft line
breaks (=\r\n or =\n) are removed. All other characters pass through
unchanged.

Returns:
The <quotedPrintableDecode> <function> <return|returns> the original
<binary file|binary data>.

Description:
Use the <quotedPrintableDecode> <function> to take a
Quoted-Printable-<encode|encoded> <string> and transform it back into
the original <binary file|binary data>.

The <quotedPrintableDecode> <function> is the <inverse> of the
<quotedPrintableEncode> <function>.

Quoted-Printable encoding is commonly used in MIME email to allow
mostly-ASCII text to survive transmission through gateways that may
alter or drop non-ASCII bytes.

For technical information about Quoted-Printable encoding, see
[RFC 2045, section 6.7](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045#section-6.7).

References: function (control structure), base64Decode (function),
quotedPrintableEncode (function), encode (glossary),
return (glossary), binary file (glossary), string (keyword),
inverse (keyword)

Tags: text processing
